fdlibm (exp and log1p)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Files:      src/zurand_fdlibm.h (derived from e_exp.c and s_log1p.c)
Copyright:  Copyright (C) 1993, 2004 by Sun Microsystems, Inc.
            All rights reserved.
License:    Permission to use, copy, modify, and distribute this software
            is freely granted, provided that this notice is preserved.
Source:     https://www.netlib.org/fdlibm/

Provides exp() and log1p() for the ziggurat's slow path, so that
rng_normal() does not depend on the platform's libm. Modified: products
that feed an addition are kept from fusing into a multiply-add, word
access uses memcpy instead of pointer casts, and a negative left shift is
done in unsigned arithmetic. The notices are preserved in the file.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
fast_prng (McFarland's modified ziggurat)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Files:      tools/generate-mcfarland-tables.py (derived from create_layers.py)
            src/zurand_engine.h, the mcf_* functions (derived from normal.h)
Copyright:  Copyright (c) 2025 Christopher D McFarland
License:    MIT
Source:     https://github.com/cd-mcfarland/fast_prng

Provides the algorithm behind rng_normal(method = "mcfarland"). Nothing is
copied verbatim: the table construction is re-implemented in mpmath at 60
digits instead of numpy long double, the 56-bit alias thresholds and the
single interpolation formula differ from the original, the normal tail uses
Marsaglia's method with zurand's fdlibm log1p() instead of the exponential
ziggurat, and every word after the first comes from zurand's per-position
retry stream. Reference: C. D. McFarland (2016), "A modified ziggurat
algorithm for generating exponentially and normally distributed
pseudorandom numbers", Journal of Statistical Computation and Simulation
86(7), 1281-1294, <doi:10.1080/00949655.2015.1060234>.

